        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/06/apples-latest-macos-updates-address-a-serious-screen-sharing-vulnerability/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2024/06/apple-hacked.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple has now published the security details for today’s macOS Tahoe, Sequoia, and Sonoma <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/06/apple-releases-security-updates-to-macos-tahoe-sequoia-and-sonoma/\">updates</a>, revealing that all three address a serious Screen Sharing vulnerability. Here is what Apple fixed.</p>",
